WEBVTT

00:32.450 --> 00:34.110
It's been seventeen years, huh?

00:34.510 --> 00:37.520
No wonder I look like a middle-aged man.

01:02.280 --> 01:08.700
hane ga shiroku hikari mabushiku tondeyuku

01:02.280 --> 01:08.700
White feathers gleam and fly away brightly

01:09.120 --> 01:15.750
kokoro dake nosete hoshii no ni

01:09.120 --> 01:15.750
Though I only want to set my heart on them

01:16.750 --> 01:23.010
tsumetai te wo nobasu todokanai... shitteru

01:16.750 --> 01:23.010
I extend my cold hands - They won't reach... I know

01:23.640 --> 01:30.730
dakedo ima furetai kimi ni

01:23.640 --> 01:30.730
But I want to touch you now

01:30.940 --> 01:36.860
natsukashii kaze ni ha ano koro no fune

01:30.940 --> 01:36.860
On that nostalgic wind - A ship from the past

01:37.270 --> 01:45.280
maboroshi ga omoide wo miseta

01:37.270 --> 01:45.280
An illusion showed me memories

01:46.350 --> 01:55.290
"wasurenai" dareka no koe ga setsunaku hibiku

01:46.350 --> 01:55.290
"I won't forget" Someone's voice echoes painfully

01:55.460 --> 02:00.380
hajimaru yokan ni furuete

01:55.460 --> 02:00.380
Trembling with a foreboding

02:00.670 --> 02:08.720
"wasuretai" negau jibun ga wakaranai

02:00.670 --> 02:08.720
"I want to forget" I cannot understand myself for hoping so

02:09.100 --> 02:18.440
matteiru yurarenagara yume hitotsu wo

02:09.100 --> 02:18.440
I shall wait while swaying, for that one dream

02:25.120 --> 02:26.790
Thank you for your purchase.

02:25.120 --> 02:31.070
Pouring Light

02:37.550 --> 02:38.800
Hey, isn't this...?

02:38.840 --> 02:41.090
This store actually sells these?

02:41.390 --> 02:43.140
They just arrived two days ago.

02:43.430 --> 02:44.810
How would you know that?

02:44.970 --> 02:46.020
Leave everything to me.

02:46.270 --> 02:48.310
I've been coming to convenience stores for 400 years.

02:48.980 --> 02:50.940
Thanks for such an obvious lie.

02:50.940 --> 02:52.860
Or was it 200 years?

02:53.020 --> 02:55.270
We didn't have convenience stores during the Edo period.

02:53.190 --> 02:53.690
The Edo period is from 1603 to 1868.

02:55.270 --> 02:57.820
Come to think of it, there might not have been any back then.

02:58.530 --> 02:59.450
Oh yeah...

02:59.780 --> 03:01.030
You'd actually know.

03:02.320 --> 03:04.120
You're going to drink all of those?!

03:05.660 --> 03:07.370
They taste great!

03:28.060 --> 03:29.270
Where's dinner?

03:29.980 --> 03:31.640
Just get out of there for now.

03:32.060 --> 03:36.480
If I were to give this to you in there, I'd feel like I'm just throwing out good food.

03:45.570 --> 03:47.280
It's just as disgusting as I thought...

03:49.120 --> 03:50.000
What's wrong?

03:50.330 --> 03:56.130
I just wondered how the evening sky would look like from here.

03:56.670 --> 03:58.000
Well...

03:58.000 --> 03:59.340
It's not that bad.

04:01.300 --> 04:02.010
But...

04:02.590 --> 04:08.010
The riverbank of the Kanami River is a far better place to enjoy the evening sky.

04:09.890 --> 04:11.020
As for the sunset...

04:11.480 --> 04:14.770
The veranda at Mizuno-san's house in Miike is the best.

04:15.900 --> 04:16.980
Well, probably.

04:18.230 --> 04:20.030
I haven't checked it out yet.

04:20.320 --> 04:26.320
But during this season, that spot must be the best since it's located between the office buildings.

04:26.780 --> 04:28.200
I see.

04:28.660 --> 04:31.040
I have try harder and get to know them better.

04:32.160 --> 04:33.410
You don't know them?

04:33.660 --> 04:34.710
Not really.

04:37.420 --> 04:38.040
And...

04:38.590 --> 04:40.050
As for the night sky...

04:40.340 --> 04:41.550
That park?

04:41.920 --> 04:42.590
Yeah.

04:42.760 --> 04:43.380
That's right.

04:52.180 --> 04:55.520
This place is much better than a garbage bin, eh?

04:57.190 --> 04:58.020
It's too spacious.

05:07.410 --> 05:10.160
Now my lost lamb, confess your sins.

05:12.400 --> 05:15.500
Your choice in onigiri is horrible.

05:16.120 --> 05:18.670
That's not a confession, but rather a complaint.

05:18.920 --> 05:22.670
In that case, forgive Takeshi for his bad taste in choosing onigiri.

05:23.880 --> 05:26.130
There's no need to confess other people's sins.

05:26.590 --> 05:28.640
You're going tomorrow, right?

05:28.930 --> 05:29.720
Where?

05:29.970 --> 05:31.180
Don't play dumb!

05:33.350 --> 05:34.520
I'm coming with you.

05:34.560 --> 05:36.440
I told you already, you don't need to come.

05:36.690 --> 05:38.310
It's not going very well, is it?

05:38.560 --> 05:40.400
I'll speak to her in person and-

05:40.400 --> 05:44.530
No, no. It's nothing so important that Mayuko-sama must bother herself with.

05:45.240 --> 05:46.280
Don't play dumb!

05:46.490 --> 05:49.160
Really, I'm fine by myself.

05:50.240 --> 05:51.620
I'm definitely going no matter what.

05:51.780 --> 05:52.370
No you aren't.

05:55.040 --> 05:57.870
After we come to terms, you'll be meeting it regardless of what you want.

06:13.720 --> 06:15.390
Just when it's our day off...

06:16.390 --> 06:17.600
You don't like the rain?

06:19.650 --> 06:21.480
I'm not too fond of it.

06:22.270 --> 06:23.900
Since you can't see the sky.

06:32.830 --> 06:35.370
So you can go outside on rainy days?

06:35.540 --> 06:36.290
Yeah.

06:36.660 --> 06:39.290
So where do you want me to take you?

06:42.710 --> 06:43.500
Here.

06:43.750 --> 06:46.090
Why would you want to come here on a rainy day like this?

06:47.970 --> 06:49.340
What are you doing?!

06:49.630 --> 06:52.680
There's nothing to lose by getting to know them beforehand, is there?

06:52.890 --> 06:54.930
I need to be mentally prepared first!

06:55.060 --> 06:55.600
Yes?

06:55.930 --> 06:57.270
Who is it?

06:59.020 --> 06:59.440
H-Hey! What are you...?

06:59.440 --> 06:59.850
H-Hey! What are you...?

06:59.850 --> 07:00.520
H-Hey! What are you...?

07:01.020 --> 07:02.310
Wait up!

07:05.730 --> 07:07.900
Hey, what did you do that for?

07:16.740 --> 07:18.620
I left my umbrella...

07:30.380 --> 07:32.380
So this is the spot?

07:33.010 --> 07:33.470
Yeah.

07:53.070 --> 07:54.740
Which season would you recommend?

07:55.160 --> 07:56.120
Autumn, I guess.

07:56.580 --> 07:58.040
The sky seems so vast.

07:58.700 --> 08:00.160
It makes me feel like I can fly.

08:04.750 --> 08:06.880
Don't you know this place better than me?

08:07.170 --> 08:07.750
Yup.

08:07.750 --> 08:09.170
I come here a lot.

08:09.630 --> 08:10.800
To kick the vending machine?

08:11.090 --> 08:12.970
I don't always kick it.

08:13.130 --> 08:13.930
Really?

08:14.300 --> 08:15.800
I used to hit it with my hand.

08:16.100 --> 08:17.390
How's that any different?

08:17.810 --> 08:21.480
But nothing would come out until I'd hit it so many times that my hand would turn all red.

08:21.480 --> 08:23.600
So you switched to your legs?

08:25.190 --> 08:28.820
It's great that tomato bean soup is sold in convenience stores now.

08:29.020 --> 08:30.730
It's great for this vending machine too.

08:30.940 --> 08:35.030
When we first met here, I thought you were a weird guy.

08:35.200 --> 08:36.120
Hey, hold on a sec!

08:36.280 --> 08:37.950
That's my line!

08:38.950 --> 08:40.200
I'm weird?

08:40.580 --> 08:41.290
What about me?

08:41.620 --> 08:44.250
Well, just about everything.

08:45.250 --> 08:47.250
Looks we grew up on different values.

08:47.840 --> 08:50.340
I don't think it's something like that...

08:54.010 --> 08:55.220
I feel like riding a boat.

09:02.060 --> 09:03.600
Why a boat out of all things?

09:04.060 --> 09:05.980
I've always wanted to ride in one before.

09:14.400 --> 09:15.860
Usually,

09:16.070 --> 09:21.160
isn't the guy supposed to get in first, help the girl in, and then ask if she's okay?

09:21.620 --> 09:22.620
How typical.

09:23.080 --> 09:24.750
Sorry, but I don't have a lot of experience in this.

09:27.370 --> 09:28.330
Are you okay?

09:30.210 --> 09:31.340
I'm fine.

09:41.640 --> 09:42.390
Are you all right?

09:43.430 --> 09:44.270
Thanks.

09:49.400 --> 09:50.520
Shouldn't I...

09:50.900 --> 09:52.070
...be the one rowing?

09:52.650 --> 09:54.780
The people at the boat shop were laughing.

09:54.940 --> 09:56.110
It's fine.

09:57.400 --> 09:59.910
Even if it's for a bit, I feel like I'm rowing under the blue sky.

10:00.370 --> 10:02.370
And I really can't do this by myself.

10:03.990 --> 10:04.660
Hey.

10:05.790 --> 10:06.870
Come over here.

10:08.870 --> 10:10.580
Hurry, hurry.

10:18.130 --> 10:18.880
Well?

10:19.430 --> 10:22.430
Doesn't it feel like being under the blue sky?

10:23.140 --> 10:23.890
Yeah.

10:24.680 --> 10:25.680
You're right.

11:05.600 --> 11:07.180
I'll keep my promise.

11:08.770 --> 11:09.560
The blue sky.

11:11.400 --> 11:13.190
I'll show it to you one day.

11:16.190 --> 11:16.690
Yeah.

11:53.190 --> 11:53.730
Here.

11:57.230 --> 11:59.070
It's wonderful!

11:59.320 --> 12:01.900
I'll teach you how to make it.

12:02.110 --> 12:04.740
Please, please. Teach me how!

12:05.950 --> 12:07.580
On one condition.

12:07.620 --> 12:08.160
Okay.

12:08.410 --> 12:12.080
If it's something I can do, please go ahead and tell me.

12:13.750 --> 12:14.500
It is.

12:18.130 --> 12:19.710
What are you doing?

12:20.260 --> 12:23.090
Coordinating the clothes I borrowed from Mana.

12:23.340 --> 12:25.590
Why don't you do it in your own room?

12:25.800 --> 12:28.100
It's so much more roomy in here.

12:28.390 --> 12:32.100
So you didn't consider the possibility of me using the living room?

12:32.310 --> 12:33.100
Yup.

12:33.850 --> 12:34.810
Good answer.

12:35.060 --> 12:36.100
Thank you.

12:37.020 --> 12:39.480
I'll be heading to the hospital now.

12:40.110 --> 12:41.610
Take care.

12:50.910 --> 12:52.160
I'll return in the evening.

12:54.500 --> 12:55.370
Takeshi.

12:57.170 --> 12:58.500
Don't push yourself.

12:59.420 --> 13:00.550
I'll be fine.

13:00.960 --> 13:03.090
You know I really hate working hard.

13:13.430 --> 13:14.640
Liar.

14:03.440 --> 14:04.530
Yorito?

14:12.950 --> 14:14.580
Thank you very much.

14:15.290 --> 14:15.830
I-I'm Ishizuki Koyori.

14:15.830 --> 14:19.080
I-I'm Ishizuki Koyori.

14:19.080 --> 14:23.000
Today I'm working undercover to carry out a secret condi-

14:23.170 --> 14:25.840
It's top secret, so I can't tell you...

14:26.210 --> 14:26.880
Umm...

14:27.090 --> 14:27.760
Well...

14:28.090 --> 14:29.380
Ishizuki?

14:30.800 --> 14:31.510
Mana?

14:31.680 --> 14:33.260
No, I'm Koyori.

14:33.760 --> 14:34.770
I'm Matsuri.

14:37.310 --> 14:38.810
Nice to meet you.

14:39.560 --> 14:40.770
Nice to meet you too.

14:47.400 --> 14:48.150
Sis.

14:50.950 --> 14:52.320
How are you feeling?

14:53.160 --> 14:53.870
Normal.

14:56.290 --> 14:58.540
Thank you for everything.

14:58.870 --> 15:00.330
You're welcome.

15:00.830 --> 15:02.500
Come back any time.

15:03.080 --> 15:03.540
Okay.

15:15.810 --> 15:16.850
What was that?

15:17.180 --> 15:19.560
Did Koyori-chan forget something?

15:25.070 --> 15:26.530
That's odd...

15:44.080 --> 15:46.090
You won't be able to run away outside this time.

15:54.850 --> 15:57.310
I just have to destroy your escape routes and corner you.

16:01.350 --> 16:03.440
Hey, wait up!

16:22.960 --> 16:26.170
Now then, where are you going to run off to?

17:30.770 --> 17:32.150
Then how about this!

17:57.630 --> 17:58.840
This is the end...

17:59.470 --> 18:00.140
Yaka.

18:47.270 --> 18:48.180
She went outside?!

18:48.640 --> 18:49.350
Impossible!

18:57.530 --> 18:58.360
I'm home.

19:02.490 --> 19:03.370
What's this...?

19:13.920 --> 19:14.920
Matsuri!

19:15.670 --> 19:16.460
Matsuri?

19:17.960 --> 19:18.760
Matsuri?

19:20.680 --> 19:21.550
Matsuri...

19:35.440 --> 19:37.360
Why didn't you kill me back then?

19:39.670 --> 19:43.570
Nevertheless, I need your life.

19:48.830 --> 19:50.620
STOP IT!

19:54.290 --> 19:55.130
Yorito!

19:56.210 --> 19:58.300
I told you not to get involved in this.

19:59.210 --> 19:59.880
Out of my way!

20:00.800 --> 20:01.590
No.

20:02.590 --> 20:04.510
Yorito, don't do this!

20:04.760 --> 20:05.640
No!

20:14.400 --> 20:16.020
I promised!

20:16.480 --> 20:18.530
That I'm going to show you the blue sky!

20:33.080 --> 20:34.620
Hey!

20:48.470 --> 20:51.060
Don't you like the rain?

20:52.890 --> 20:55.560
I've come to like it... just a bit.

21:00.690 --> 21:01.400
Matsuri?!

21:02.610 --> 21:05.360
Why did you leave your door wide-open if nobody's at home?

21:05.570 --> 21:07.780
And what are you two doing here...?

21:15.620 --> 21:19.210
But why keep it a secret from Yorito-san?

21:21.800 --> 21:23.590
Because it's something important.

21:29.010 --> 21:32.100
After you're done, I'll sneak back in and return it.

21:33.350 --> 21:37.230
I'm sure Matsuri-san will help me if she's still there.

21:38.440 --> 21:43.280
Matsuri-san is Yorito-san's friend, and she's really a kind person.

21:43.650 --> 21:47.570
She treated me nicely, even though I was trespassing.

21:47.570 --> 21:48.620
She even gave me a gift.

21:50.070 --> 21:52.450
Huh? Where did it go?

21:52.740 --> 21:55.290
I'm sure I brought it...

22:13.310 --> 22:21.980
iro aseta page no kioku hitomi tojireba yomigaeru

22:13.310 --> 22:21.980
Memories on a faded page, they revive when I close my eyes

22:22.400 --> 22:31.160
adokenai shoujo no inori
habatakeyo kibou no sora he

22:22.400 --> 22:31.160
Prayers of an innocent girl
Fly away to the sky of hope

22:31.280 --> 22:35.580
nageku mamonaku  toki wa nagareru

22:31.280 --> 22:35.580
With no time to regret, time will flow

22:35.870 --> 22:40.670
hitori tachidomaru kedo

22:35.870 --> 22:40.670
Even though I stand alone

22:41.920 --> 22:47.430
yume mamoru shirabe  kuchizu samuno

22:41.920 --> 22:47.430
A tune to protect your dreams, I sing to myself

22:47.590 --> 22:51.930
hitobito ga nemuri ni tsukeba

22:47.590 --> 22:51.930
When people go into slumber

22:52.140 --> 22:59.850
mata au hi no negai tsumugeru deshou  ai no ito

22:52.140 --> 22:59.850
Their wish to unite can be woven. The thread of love

23:00.150 --> 23:10.280
yasashisa wo sasou  otogibanashi anata kara osowatta no yo

23:00.150 --> 23:10.280
Fairy tales that elicit kindness I learned that from you

23:10.450 --> 23:20.210
modorimashou  sotto ano koro no omoi ni

23:10.450 --> 23:20.210
Let us return gently to the memories of those times

23:29.970 --> 23:44.970
Next Time

23:29.970 --> 23:44.970
Blood of a Sacrifice

23:30.800 --> 23:33.390
Aono-san, please teach me origami.

23:33.590 --> 23:34.760
All right.

23:35.140 --> 23:36.760
By the way, what are you teaching me?

23:37.020 --> 23:37.640
A crane...

23:37.850 --> 23:39.770
Even I know how to make that.

23:40.230 --> 23:41.810
...being folded by Koyori.
